# PropertyOS Vision Document

Version: 1.0
Status: Draft
Author: Andrew Evboifo
Date: July 2026

---

# Vision

PropertyOS is aimed to be a modern cloud-based property management platform designed to simplify the day-to-day operations of landlords and property management companies.

The platform provides a single system for managing residential and commercial properties, tenants, leases, maintenance requests, payments, documents, and operational reporting.

My vision is to eliminate fragmented workflows by replacing spreadsheets, paper records, disconnected software, and manual communication with one intuitive platform that scales from individual landlords to large property management organizations.

---

# Problem Statement

Many landlords and property managers still rely on multiple disconnected tools:

- Excel spreadsheets
- Paper lease agreements
- Email
- Phone calls
- Text messages
- Accounting software
- Calendar applications

This results in:

- Lost information
- Delayed maintenance
- Missed rent payments
- Duplicate data
- Poor communication
- Limited reporting
- Increased operational costs

As portfolios grow, these inefficiencies become increasingly difficult to manage.

---

# Mission

To build an intuitive, secure, and scalable property management platform that enables property professionals to manage their entire business from one centralized system.

---

# Target Users

Primary Users

- Independent landlords
- Property managers
- Property management companies

Secondary Users

- Tenants
- Maintenance technicians
- Vendors
- Building owners
- System administrators

---

# Core Business Goals

PropertyOS should enable users to:

- Manage properties and units
- Manage tenant information
- Create and manage leases
- Track rent payments
- Handle maintenance requests
- Store documents securely
- Communicate with tenants
- Generate operational reports
- Monitor occupancy
- Track financial performance

---

# Product Principles

The system should always be:

Simple
Easy for non-technical users to operate.

Reliable
Business-critical information should always be accurate.

Secure
Protect sensitive tenant and financial information.

Scalable
Support portfolios ranging from one property to thousands.

Maintainable
Designed with clean architecture for future growth.

Modern
Provide an intuitive user experience across desktop and mobile devices.

---

# Long-Term Vision

PropertyOS will evolve beyond traditional property management software by incorporating automation, intelligent reporting, predictive maintenance insights, AI-assisted workflows, and integrations with third-party financial and communication platforms.

The long-term objective is to become a complete operating system for property management businesses.

---

# Success Metrics

A successful MVP should allow a property manager to:

- Create an organization
- Add properties
- Add units
- Register tenants
- Create leases
- Record rent payments
- Submit maintenance requests
- Generate basic reports

without requiring external spreadsheets or manual record keeping.

---

# Out of Scope (Version 1)

The initial release will not include:

- AI automation
- Online banking integrations
- Tax filing
- Accounting software synchronization
- IoT smart building integrations
- Utility billing
- Marketing websites
- CRM functionality

These features may be considered in future releases.
